<title>SWEDEN: Gammon wins 375 mln NOK Hong Kong order.</title>
<headline>Gammon wins 375 mln NOK Hong Kong order.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Norwegian construction and engineering group Kvaerner ASA said on Tuesday its half-owned Hong Kong subsidiary Gammon Construction won an order worth 375 million crowns ($48.8 million) from Ka Chee Co Ltd in Hong Kong.  </p>
<p>The order is for work on a commercial office tower, Olympia Plaza, on Kings Road in Hong Kong, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Gammon has already finished the foundation work for the building, which will be ready in December 1998.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
